    "q-213403": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213403",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following integers has a multiplicative inverse modulo $30?$\n\nI. $7$\n\nII. $15$\n\nIII. $21$",
      "worked_solution": "An integer $a$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $n$ if and only if $a$ and $n$ are coprime, i.e., $\\text{gcd}(a,n)=1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- $7$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $30$ since $\\text{gcd}(7,30)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $15$ does *not* have a multiplicative inverse modulo $30$ since $\\text{gcd}(15,30)=15\\ne 1.\\,\\,\\times $\n\n- $21$ does *not* have a multiplicative inverse modulo $30$ since $\\text{gcd}(21,30)=3\\ne 1.\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
